DOCTYPE Declaration: Defines the document type and version of HTML.
HTML Tag with Language Attribute: Specifies the language of the document.

Head Section:
Meta Tags: Set the character encoding and viewport settings for responsive design.
Title Tag: Sets the title of the web page.
Bootstrap CSS Link: Links to Bootstrap CSS for styling.
Bootstrap JS Script: Links to Bootstrap JS for interactive components.
Style Tag: Contains custom CSS for styling the form, message IDs, body background, and placeholders for additional styling.

Style Tag:

Explanation:

.my-form:

Styles the form that is fixed at the bottom of the page.
position: Fixed to ensure it stays at the bottom.
bottom, right, left: Sets the distance from the respective edges.
width: Calculates the width to fit within the given space.
Commented Out Sections:

These sections are enclosed in /* */, which means they are comments and not currently executed by the browser.
Custom Message Styling:
.my-message: Intended to style the user's messages with a red background.
.other-message: Intended to style other users' messages with a light red background.
Currently commented out due to non-functionality, but indicate intended functionality.
body:

Sets the background color of the entire page to light blue.
.msg-id:

Styles the message ID text.
font-size: Sets the size of the text.
position: Absolutely positions it within its container.
right, bottom: Sets the distance from the right and bottom edges.
color: Sets the color with some transparency.
